  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual message as the source of divisive rhetoric",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material ('yes i'm trying to divide the country i'm dividing the illegals from the actual citizens') which is overlaid on the image of Donald Trump. The meme implies that the user (as the viewer) is identifying with or attributing the divisive rhetoric to the political figure, thereby projecting the user's own perspective or judgment onto the text and the visual of Trump. This projection is not explicit through deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me' in the text itself, but is inferred from the meme's structure: the viewer is positioned as the one interpreting the text as a direct statement from Trump, and thus the user is projected onto the scene as the one who is 'seeing' or 'understanding' the divisive nature of the policy. The projection is onto the textual material which frames the political figure's actions.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
  "extractedFrom": "47905",
